Vendored regression test files from postgis_tiger_geocoder
============================================================

Source:   https://gitea.osgeo.org/postgis/postgis_tiger_geocoder
          (paths: src/regress/*)
Mirror:   https://github.com/ericmanning/postgis_tiger_geocoder
License:  GPL v2 (same as us_geocoder)
Copyright the PostGIS project / individual contributors.

These files are vendored verbatim — no modifications — so the parity
harness in scripts/parity/ can compare our geocoder's output against
PostGIS's reference behavior.

Files:
  geocode_regress.sql                       — input test queries
  geocode_regress                           — expected outputs from PG
  pagc_normalize_address_regress.sql        — input parser test queries
  pagc_normalize_address_regress            — expected outputs from PG
  pagc_normalize_address_desired_regress    — aspirational outputs (PG TODO list)
  reverse_geocode_regress.sql               — input reverse-geocode queries
  reverse_geocode_regress                   — expected outputs from PG
  regress.sql                               — runner (sets debug flags, includes others)

The expected outputs were captured against a specific TIGER vintage
(likely 2010-era) using PG's PAGC standardizer rules of that time. Exact
numeric parity with TIGER 2025 + the current us_address_standardizer
community extension is not expected — block boundaries shift, addresses
get added, PAGC rule files evolve. The harness reports diffs; engineers
investigating divergence claims interpret them.
